{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"rebar-implement plan-review claim gate BLOCKED this story with 7 critical findings that collapse into two design flaws. (A) Merge mechanism [findings 1,2,5]: the heal's 'merge=union driver' is EXPLICITLY FORBIDDEN in this codebase — init.py _GITATTRIBUTES documents 'merge=union is WRONG here — it line-unions JSON into invalid JSON'. Remediable: rebar's event dirs are uuid-named and never collide, so a plain multi-parent (--allow-unrelated-histories/octopus) merge is already lossless; the only shared mutable files (.bridge_state/*) already use merge=ours (a derived cache the reconciler rebuilds). (B) S3 object operations [findings 3,4,6,7 — NO suggested fix, premise-level]: the plan routes the DOCTOR lock marker (conditional-put/TTL/steal), bundle enumeration, and per-head bundle deletion 'through the helper's own S3 remote' with 'no direct S3 SDK use' (AC line 6), but git-remote-s3 is a git remote-helper SUBPROCESS speaking only the git protocol (ref list/fetch/push) — it exposes NO API for arbitrary S3 object ops or a conditional-put lock/TTL, and rebar's only helper touchpoint is require_s3_helper() (a PATH+version>=0.3.2 check). The plan's S3-ops foundation rests on a capability that does not exist. Recommended pivot (needs confirmation): have the OPTIONAL s3_doctor.py use boto3 directly — boto3 ships transitively with git-remote-s3, so this adds NO hard dep to CORE rebar (same optionality contract as the [s3] extra) — implementing the DOCTOR lock as rebar's own IfNoneMatch conditional-put S3 object and doing bundle list/delete via boto3. This reverses the story's 'route everything through the helper' premise, so surfacing for a design decision rather than a unilateral rewrite. Stories 2b05 + 8970 are DONE (landed + closed); this story and b014 remain open."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786171617638478001,"uuid":"c6603e82-9dfd-4b06-814d-8fd5362b7c9a"}